        "username": "fjur",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/{size}/4849_2.png",
        "created_at": "2023-10-24T02:15:18.089Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Lots of the time, I’d imagine, folks simply do what the rulebook says and have the Heroes take their turns going clockwise / counter-clockwise around the table. But what about the times when y’all don’t do that, like when you’re playing solo or multi-handed, or the players simply decide to not base the turn order on where everyone is sitting?</p>\n<p>(As I’ve likely said on here before, I usually play 2 player / 3-4 Hero games, so we don’t just go in physical table order, 'cause then one or both players would be taking two Hero turns in a row; instead we alternate.)</p>\n<p>What common methods do you use to choose which Hero goes when? Most commonly, I’ll just fall back on a heuristic that is simply “the more support effects a Hero has the sooner they should act,”*  but I feel like that are probably some more nuanced things to take into consideration too.</p>\n<p>So, what do y’all think? How do you do it? Any tips or suggestions?</p>\n<p>*With some exceptions, of course — such as Unity, Guise, or DW Mr. Fixer going near the end.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2023-10-24T02:15:18.089Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
